  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-two-song set at the Wonder Ballroom in Portland, Oregon, on Tuesday, October 21, 2008 [1]. This recording, captured and transferred by Carl Shoemaker, is the only archived performance of this specific show [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as \"Have to Explode,\" \"Palmcorder Yajna,\" and \"How to Embrace a Swamp Creature\" [4]. Listeners noted that the band played \"secret songs\" during the performance, a topic that generated significant discussion in the comments [2]. One reviewer recalled that the frontman stated the songs were not for request but could be shared if he felt like it, which others interpreted as approval for the archive upload [2][7]. Another listener clarified that track thirteen is titled \"Supergenesis\" and is a collaboration, while track fourteen is an instrumental extension rather than a distinct song [6]. The audio quality is praised for having very little crowd noise, allowing the music and banter to shine clearly [8]. The set also features a Morrissey cover and a song dedicated to a stepfather [4]. Although some listeners initially questioned the inclusion of the private material, the consensus is that the recording is fantastic and the songs are now part of the archive [8]. This performance is the 129th in the performer’s collection on the platform [9]. The recording is rated 3.14 out of 5 by seven listeners [1].",
